(Ravik statement on rail capacity for Orvan grain) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Ravik government issued this statement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Rail movements through the Ravik Rail Link have risen since the Orvan) Tj
T*
(corridor ended. The link is carrying grain that would otherwise have gone by) Tj
T*
(sea.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] "The rail link covers all of the exports Orvan has lost," said Sana Okafor,) Tj
T*
(the Ravik trade minister.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The government says shippers should book rail capacity early.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The statement was issued after a meeting between the Ravik government and) Tj
T*
(rail operators. It is short on detail: it does not give the volume moved, the) Tj
T*
(share of the lost trade carried, or the tariff charged. The minister's office) Tj
T*
(says the purpose was to reassure buyers that a land route exists.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The statement was read out at a briefing and later posted on the ministry's) Tj
T*
(notice board. It does not name the rail operators who attended, and it does not) Tj
T*
(describe the terms on which space is allocated. Buyers who need a booking have) Tj
T*
(been told to approach the link directly. The government says it will issue a) Tj
T*
(further statement if capacity changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] The statement does not give volumes or tariffs.) Tj
